 "capsule": "This 'Mexico' denotes the consolidated federal republic from the 1867 Restored Republic under Benito Juárez, following the fall of Maximilian's Second Mexican Empire, through the Porfiriato, the 1910 Revolution, seven decades of PRI-dominated one-party rule, and the democratic alternation beginning with Vicente Fox's 2000 election. It remains a federal presidential republic under the 1917 constitution into the 2020s. This modern federal state is distinct from the 1836–1846 unitary Centralist Republic sharing this Wikidata identifier.",
